PS5 GPU on 7.3.1 + rmux shitshow: thermal governor

- GPU clock governor with a temperature limit (Borchev, #66; ps5_gpufreq.temp_limit, 85 C by default), registered
  by amdgpu. rmux's devfreq ps5-gpufreq has no thermal limit and stays disabled (CONFIG_PS5_GPUFREQ)
- Pro (Viola firmware): gpu_metrics reported as unsupported (no SMU metrics table)
- The overlay's GPU load and temperature come with the display stack (amdgpu_dm.c)
---
diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c
index 1021dcc5f..52ab4c8d7 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/amdgpu/amdgpu_device.c
@@ -3746,9 +3746,8 @@ static int amdgpu_device_sys_interface_init(struct amdgpu_device *adev)
 	/* A Pro without Viola firmware loses its SMU mailbox. */
 	if (adev->asic_type == CHIP_CYAN_SKILLFISH &&
 	    (!amdgpu_is_viola(adev) || amdgpu_ps5_viola_fw(adev)))
-		adev->ps5_gpufreq = platform_device_register_data(adev->dev, "ps5-gpufreq",
-								  PLATFORM_DEVID_NONE,
-								  NULL, 0);
+		adev->ps5_gpufreq = ps5_gpufreq_register(adev->dev,
+							 amdgpu_fence_ps5_busy_ns);
 #endif
 
 	return r;
